{"collection":{"version":"1.1","href":"http://images-api.nasa.gov/search?q=Gemini+Earth+view&media_type=image&year_start=1965&year_end=1966&page_size=25","items":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18752/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-03-23T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-18752 (23 March 1965) --- View of a cloudy part of Earth as seen from the Gemini-3 spacecraft while in orbit.","keywords":["EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","GEMINI 3 FLIGHT"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-18752","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-3 - EARTH - SKY VIEW - MADAGASCAR (MALAGASY)"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18752/s65-18752~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":116000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18752/s65-18752~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":29000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18752/s65-18752~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":29000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18752/s65-18752~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":309000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18752/s65-18752~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45763/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-08-21T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-45763 (21-29 Aug. 1965) --- View of the lower tip of Baja, California and Bahia de la Paz taken from the Gemini-5 spacecraft in orbit over Earth.","keywords":["EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","GEMINI 5 FLIGHT"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-45763","title":"GEMINI-V - EARTH-SKY VIEW - BAJA, CA - OUTER SPACE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45763/s65-45763~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1271,"size":176000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45763/s65-45763~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":635,"size":47000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45763/s65-45763~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":635,"size":47000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45763/s65-45763~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1906,"size":385000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45763/s65-45763~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-34661/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-06-01T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-34661 (3-7 June 1965) --- Among the photographs of Earth's terrain taken from the Gemini-4 spacecraft during its orbital mission was this view of the southeastern tip of the Arabian Peninsula with the Gulf of Oman at upper right. Seif dunes (sand) at lower left. This picture was taken with a modified 70mm Hasselblad camera, using Eastman color film, ASA 64 at a setting of 250th of a second at f/11. Dr. Paul Lowman Jr., NASA geologist, was in charge of the Synoptic Terrain Photography.","keywords":["EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","GEMINI 4 FLIGHT"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-34661","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-4 - EARTH-SKY VIEW"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-34661/s65-34661~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":220000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-34661/s65-34661~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":52000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-34661/s65-34661~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":52000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-34661/s65-34661~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":504000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-34661/s65-34661~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45717/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-08-21T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-45717 (21-29 Aug. 1965) --- View of the Himalayas and Northern India photographed from the Gemini-5 spacecraft in orbit over Earth.","keywords":["EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","GEMINI 5 FLIGHT"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-45717","title":"EARTH-SKY - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-5 (70mm Hasselblad)"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45717/s65-45717~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":319000,"height":1239},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45717/s65-45717~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":102000,"height":619},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45717/s65-45717~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":102000,"height":619},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45717/s65-45717~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1919,"size":623000,"height":1858},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45717/s65-45717~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45731/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-08-21T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-45731 (21-29 Aug. 1965) --- View of the Gulf of Tonkin, China and the Luichow Peninsula photographed from the Gemini-5 spacecraft in orbit over Earth.","keywords":["EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","GEMINI 5 FLIGHT"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-45731","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-5 - EARTH SKY (70MM HASSELBLAD)"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45731/s65-45731~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1274,"size":228000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45731/s65-45731~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":637,"size":66000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45731/s65-45731~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":637,"size":66000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45731/s65-45731~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1912,"size":472000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-45731/s65-45731~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61777/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-07T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-61777 (8 Dec. 1965) --- Close-up view of a laser transmitter unit which is being used for the Gemini-7 Optical Communication (MSC-4) experiment. Astronauts Frank Borman, command pilot; and James A. Lovell Jr., pilot, are now orbiting Earth in NASA's Gemini-7 spacecraft. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-61777","title":"EQUIPMENT - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-6"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61777/s65-61777~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1030,"size":99000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61777/s65-61777~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":515,"size":30000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61777/s65-61777~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":515,"size":30000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61777/s65-61777~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1545,"size":223000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61777/s65-61777~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-21520/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-03-23T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-21520 (23 March 1965) --- Distant view showing the successful launching of the first manned Gemini flight. The Gemini-Titan 3 (GT-3) lifted off Pad 19, at the Kennedy Space Center (KSC) at 9:24 a.m. (EST), March 23, 1965. The Gemini-3 spacecraft \"Molly Brown\" carried astronauts Virgil I. Grissom, command pilot, and John W. Young, pilot, on three successful orbits of Earth.","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S65-21520","title":"LIFTOFF - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-3 - DISTANT VIEW - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-21520/S65-21520~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":102000,"height":578},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-21520/S65-21520~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":27000,"height":289},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-21520/S65-21520~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":27000,"height":289},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-21520/S65-21520~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63517/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-11-13T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-63517 (13 Nov. 1966) --- The Gulf of California area as seen from the Gemini-12 spacecraft during its 30th revolution of Earth. Baja California Sur is the peninsula on the left. At lower left is the mainland of Mexico. A 100-foot tether line connects the Agena Target Docking Vehicle with the Gemini-12 spacecraft. View is looking south. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["GEMINI 12 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-63517","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-12 - EARTH SKY - AGENA ON TETHER - OUTER SPACE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63517/s66-63517~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":146000,"height":1267},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63517/s66-63517~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":43000,"height":633},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63517/s66-63517~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":43000,"height":633},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63517/s66-63517~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":304000,"height":1900},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63517/s66-63517~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18740/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-03-23T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-18740 (23 March 1965) --- Astronaut John W. Young took this picture during the second orbit of the Gemini-Titan 3 three-orbit mission as the spacecraft \"Molly Brown\" passed over Northern Mexico at an altitude of 90 miles. The light-brown circular area at the lower right is the Sonoran Desert. The lower portion of the picture is Mexico, and the upper part is California. Young used a hand-held modified 70mm Hasselblad camera with color film. The lens setting was 250th of a second at f/11.","keywords":["EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","GEMINI 3 FLIGHT"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-18740","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-3 - EARTH- SKY VIEW"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18740/s65-18740~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":129000,"height":1278},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18740/s65-18740~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":38000,"height":639},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18740/s65-18740~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":38000,"height":639},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18740/s65-18740~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":277000,"height":1917},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18740/s65-18740~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18759/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-03-23T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-18759 (23 March 1965) --- Astronaut John W. Young took this picture of clouds over the Indian Ocean during the Gemini-Titan 3 three-orbit mission on March 23, 1965. Young used a hand-held modified 70mm Hasselblad camera with color film. The lens setting was 250th of a second at f/11.","keywords":["EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","GEMINI 3 FLIGHT"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-18759","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-3 - EARTH - SKY VIEWS"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18759/s65-18759~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1268,"size":56000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18759/s65-18759~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":634,"size":15000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18759/s65-18759~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":634,"size":15000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18759/s65-18759~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1903,"size":168000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18759/s65-18759~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63830/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-05T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-63830 (5 Dec. 1965) --- Algeria, south-southeast of the Colomb Bechar area, as seen from the National Aeronautics and Space Administration's Gemini-7 spacecraft. Sand dunes are 200 to 300 feet high in the Grand Erg Occidental area. The Quod Sacura River can be seen in the upper left corner. The white spot in the middle of the picture is the Sebcha el Malah salt beds. It should be noted that the area had just experienced very heavy rains (first in many years) and the stream and salt flat are inundated. This photograph was taken with a modified 70mm Hasselblad camera, with Eastman Kodak, Ektachrome MS (S.O. 217) color film. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["ALGERIA","RAINS","DRYING","LAKES"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-63830","title":"Algeria- Gemini 7, Earth-Sky View"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63830/s65-63830~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":190000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63830/s65-63830~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":48000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63830/s65-63830~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":48000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63830/s65-63830~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":415000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63830/s65-63830~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-34659/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-06-03T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-34659 (3-7 June 1965) --- Among the many photographs taken from the Gemini-4 spacecraft during its orbital flight around Earth was this view of the Hahramaut Plateau on the southern portion of the Arabian Peninsula. The Wadi Hahramaut is in the foreground; with the Gulf of Aden (dark blue). This photograph was made with a modified 70mm Hasselblad camera, using Eastman color film, ASA 64, at a lens setting of 250th of a second at f/11.","keywords":["EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","GEMINI 4 FLIGHT"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-34659","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-4 - EARTH SKY"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-34659/s65-34659~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1276,"size":239000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-34659/s65-34659~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":638,"size":68000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-34659/s65-34659~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":638,"size":68000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-34659/s65-34659~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1914,"size":489000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-34659/s65-34659~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-54455/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-09-14T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-54455 (13 Sept. 1966) --- Astronaut Richard F. Gordon Jr., Gemini-11 pilot, attaches a tether line from his spacecraft to the Agena Target Docking Vehicle (ATDV) during a spacewalk. This view was taken over the Atlantic Ocean at approximately 160 miles above Earth on Sept. 13, 1966. With the aid of the ATDV, Gordon and astronaut Charles (Pete) Conrad Jr., command pilot, set a new altitude record of 750 miles during the GT-11 mission.  Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S66-54455","photographer":"N/A","title":"GT-11 - EARTH SKY - DOCKING"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-54455/S66-54455~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":56000,"height":867},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-54455/S66-54455~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":21000,"height":433},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-54455/S66-54455~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":21000,"height":433},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-54455/S66-54455~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":107000,"height":1301},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-54455/S66-54455~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54563/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-09-14T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-54563 (14 Sept. 1966) --- View of the Gulf Coast area from Atchafalaya Bay to Apalachicola, including the mouth of the Mississippi River, Mobile Bay, New Orleans, Louisiana, and Pensacola, Florida, as seen from the Gemini-11 spacecraft during its 29th revolution of Earth. This photo was taken near sunrise. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["COASTS","EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","GEMINI 11 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","GEMINI SPACECRAFT","GULFS","ONBOARD ACTIVITIES","PHOTOGRAPHY"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-54563","title":"Gulf Coast from from Atchafalaya Bay to Apalachicola seen from Gemini 11"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54563/s66-54563~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1270,"size":172000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54563/s66-54563~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":635,"size":51000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54563/s66-54563~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":635,"size":51000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54563/s66-54563~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1905,"size":363000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54563/s66-54563~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63486/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-11-13T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-63486 (13 Nov. 1966) --- Iran, Trucial Coast, Oman, Zagros Mountains, and Qishm Island (large island at lower right), as seen from the Gemini-12 spacecraft during its 25th revolution of Earth. Gulf of Oman is large body of water at left and the Persian Gulf is body of water at right. View is looking east. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["GEMINI 12 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-63486","title":"GT-12 - EARTH SKY -  IRAN, TRUCIAL COAST"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63486/s66-63486~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1219,"size":151000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63486/s66-63486~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":609,"size":37000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63486/s66-63486~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":609,"size":37000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63486/s66-63486~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1829,"size":372000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63486/s66-63486~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63440/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-11-12T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-63440 (12 Nov. 1966) --- Area of northwestern Mexico as seen from the Gemini-12 spacecraft during its 16th revolution of Earth. View is looking northwest. Body of water in the foreground is the Gulf of California. Pacific Ocean is in the background. Peninsula in center of picture is Baja California. States of Sonora (upper right) and Sinaloa (lower center) of Mexican mainland is in right foreground. City of Guaymas, Sonora, is near the center of the picture. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["GEMINI 12 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-63440","title":"GT-12 - EARTH SKY -  NORTHWESTERN MEXICO"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63440/s66-63440~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1263,"size":131000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63440/s66-63440~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":631,"size":36000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63440/s66-63440~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":631,"size":36000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63440/s66-63440~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1895,"size":296000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63440/s66-63440~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63136/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-16T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-63136 (16 Dec. 1965) --- Shark Bay area on the western coast of Western Australia as seen from the Gemini-6 spacecraft during its 16th revolution of Earth. City of Carnarven, where NASA has a tracking station, is located near the bottom of picture in lower left corner, near mouth of stream. Indian Ocean is body of water at upper right. South is toward top of picture. Photo credit: NASA or National Aeronautics and Space Administration","keywords":["GEMINI 6 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-63136","title":"GEMINI-6 - EARTH-SKY VIEW - AUSTRALIA - OUTER SPACE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63136/s65-63136~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1231,"size":198000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63136/s65-63136~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":615,"size":55000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63136/s65-63136~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":615,"size":55000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63136/s65-63136~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1847,"size":435000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63136/s65-63136~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-18741/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-03-23T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-18741 (23 March 1965) --- Astronaut John W. Young took this picture during the Gemini-Titan 3 three-orbit mission as the spacecraft \"Molly Brown\" passed over Northern Mexico. The large light-brown area is the Sonoran Desert. The Colorado River runs from upper right to lower left. The lower portion of the picture is Mexico, the upper left is California, and the upper right is Arizona. The altitude of the spacecraft was 90 miles. Young used a hand-held modified 70mm Hasselblad camera with color film. The lens setting was 250th of a second at f/11.","keywords":["EARTH ORBITS"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S65-18741","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-3 - EARTH-SKY VIEWS - CA"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-18741/S65-18741~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":189000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-18741/S65-18741~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":51000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-18741/S65-18741~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":51000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-18741/S65-18741~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":442000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-18741/S65-18741~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63849/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-08T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-63849 (8 Dec. 1965) --- The eastern Mediterranean area as seen from the National Aeronautics and Space Administration's Gemini-7 spacecraft. The Nile Delta in Egypt is at bottom. The Suez Canal, Gulf of Suez and Red Sea are in the center of the photograph. The Sinai Peninsula is in the upper right corner of the picture. The body of water at the top edge of the photograph is the Gulf of Aqaba. The Dead Sea can be seen at top center. Israel, Palestine, Jordan and Syria are also at top center. The Island of Cyprus is at extreme left. Astronauts Frank Borman and James A. Lovell Jr. took this picture using a modified 70mm Hasselblad camera, with Eastman Kodak, Ektachrome MS (S.O. 217) color film. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","GEMINI 7 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-63849","title":"GEMINI-7 - EARTH-SKY VIEW - MIDDLE-EAST AREA - OUTER SPACE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63849/s65-63849~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":256000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63849/s65-63849~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":76000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63849/s65-63849~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":76000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63849/s65-63849~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":517000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63849/s65-63849~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18750/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-03-23T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-18750 (23 March 1965) --- Astronaut John W. Young took this picture over eastern Africa during the Gemini-Titan 3 three-orbit mission on March 23, 1965. The altitude of the Gemini spacecraft \"Molly Brown\" was 90 miles. Young used a hand-held modified 70mm Hasselblad camera with color film. The lens setting was 250th of a second at f/11.","keywords":["EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","GEMINI 3 FLIGHT"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-18750","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-3 - EARTH - SKY VIEW - AFRICA"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18750/s65-18750~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":88000,"height":1203},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18750/s65-18750~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":26000,"height":601},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18750/s65-18750~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":26000,"height":601},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18750/s65-18750~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":210000,"height":1805},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-18750/s65-18750~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-38290/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-06-05T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-38290 (5 June 1966) --- The north coastal area of Peru looking southeast across the Andes Mountains as seen from the National Aeronautics and Space Administration's Gemini-9A spacecraft. The body of water is the Pacific Ocean. The image was taken with a modified 70mm Hasselblad camera, using Eastman Kodak, Ektachrome MS (S.O. 217) color film. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["ANDES MOUNTAINS (SOUTH AMERICA)","COASTS","GEMINI SPACERAFT","NASA PROGRAMS","PERU"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-38290","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-9 - EARTH-SKY VIEW - PERU - OUTER SPACE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-38290/s66-38290~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1279,"size":188000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-38290/s66-38290~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":639,"size":52000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-38290/s66-38290~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":639,"size":52000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-38290/s66-38290~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1918,"size":407000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-38290/s66-38290~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-65257/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-07T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-65257 (4-18 Dec. 1965) --- Sunrise and Earth's limb, as photographed by astronauts Frank Borman and James A. Lovell Jr. during their Earth-orbital 14-day mission in the Gemini-7 (GT-7) spacecraft. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","GEMINI 7 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-65257","title":"GEMINI-7 - EARTH-SKY VIEW - LIMB - OUTER SPACE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-65257/s65-65257~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":54000,"height":1215},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-65257/s65-65257~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":13000,"height":607},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-65257/s65-65257~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":13000,"height":607},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-65257/s65-65257~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":138000,"height":1823},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-65257/s65-65257~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54530/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-09-14T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-54530 --- Libyan Desert area of Sudan, foreground, and the United Arab Republic (Egypt), at lower left, as seen from the orbiting Gemini-11 spacecraft at an altitude of 300 nautical miles during its 27th revolution of Earth. In view is the Nile River from Biba in Egypt to Khartoum in the Sudan. The Red Sea is in the background. At upper left is the Arabian Peninsula. At top right is Ethiopia. Note L-band antenna of the Agena Target Vehicle. Taken with a modified 70mm Hasselblad camera, using Eastman Kodak, Ektachrome, MS (S.O. 368) color film. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["GEMINI 11 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-54530","photographer":"N/A","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-11 - HIGH APOGEE - EARTH SKY"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54530/s66-54530~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":156000,"height":1278},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54530/s66-54530~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":45000,"height":639},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54530/s66-54530~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":45000,"height":639},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54530/s66-54530~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1919,"size":333000,"height":1917},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54530/s66-54530~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-37910/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-06-03T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-37910 (3 June 1966) --- The Mississippi River delta, and Gulf coasts of Louisiana, Mississippi, Alabama and Florida as seen from the Gemini-9 spacecraft during its first revolution of Earth. The Florida peninsula is seen at upper right corner of the picture. Lake Pontchartrain is a lower left. New Orleans is located between the lake and the U-shaped bend in the river. Large bay at top left center is Mobile Bay. The next bay to the east is Pensacola Bay. Cape San Blas near Apalachicola, Florida, is the point of land at top center of the picture. Note alluvial deposit at the mouths of the Mississippi. The image was taken with a modified 70mm Hasselblad camera, using Eastman Kodak, Ektachrome MS (S.O. 217) color film. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","GEMINI 9 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-37910","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-9A - EARTH-SKY VIEW - NEW ORLEANS - OUTER SPACE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-37910/s66-37910~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":166000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-37910/s66-37910~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":47000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-37910/s66-37910~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":47000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-37910/s66-37910~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":357000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-37910/s66-37910~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61788/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-10T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-61788 (For release: 11 Dec. 1965) --- Close-up view of equipment which will be used in the D-8 (Radiation in Spacecraft) experiment on the National Aeronautics and Space Administration's Gemini-6 spaceflight. This experiment is designed to make highly accurate measurements of the absorbed dose rate of radiation which penetrates the Gemini spacecraft, and determine the spatial distribution of dose levels inside the spacecraft particularly in the crew area. This is experimentation of the U.S. Air Force Weapons Laboratory, Kirtland AFB, N.M.   LOWER LEFT: The second ionization chamber, this one is unshielded. This chamber can be removed from its bracket by the astronaut who will periodically take measurements at various locations in the spacecraft. Nearby is Passive Dosimeter Unit which is one of five small packets each containing a standard pocket ionization chamber, gamma electron sensitive film, glass needles and thermo luminescent dosimeters which are mounted at various locations in the cabin. UPPER LEFT: Photo illustrates how ionization chamber can be removed from bracket for measurements. LOWER RIGHT: Shield of bulb-shaped chamber will be removed (shown in photo) as the spacecraft passes through the South Atlantic anomaly, the area where the radiation belt dips closest to Earth's surface. UPPER RIGHT: Dome-shaped object is shield covering one of two Tissue Equivalent Ionization Chambers (sensors) which will read out continuously the instantaneous rate at which dose is delivered during the flight. This chamber is mounted permanently. The information will be recorded aboard the spacecraft, and will also be received directly by ground stations. This chamber is shielded to simulate the amount of radiation the crew members are receiving beneath their skin. Photo credit: NASA or National Aeronautics and Space Administration","keywords":["BRACKETS","DOSIMETERS","IONIZATION CHAMBERS","SPACEBORNE EXPERIMENTS"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-61788","title":"CHAMBER - IONIZATION - EXPERIMENT - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-6 EQUIPMENT - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61788/s65-61788~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":191000,"height":1051},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61788/s65-61788~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":57000,"height":525},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61788/s65-61788~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":57000,"height":525},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61788/s65-61788~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":439000,"height":1576},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61788/s65-61788~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]}],"metadata":{"total_hits":25}}}